"""Auto-generated rugarch reference data for standalone variance-model tests.

Regenerate with:
    Rscript copulax/tests/_r_reference/generate_garch_standalone_reference.R \
        > copulax/tests/_r_reference/garch_standalone_reference_data.py

rugarch 1.5.5 on R 4.6.0.

Layer-1 convention: rugarch fixes the leading max(p, q) conditional
variances at mean(residuals^2) (rec.init="all") and recurses from
index max(p, q); copulax reproduces this with init="squared". The
stored `sigma2` is the full fitted conditional-variance path and
`loglikelihood` the reported LLH -- both matched two-sided at
rtol <= 1e-8 in test_timeseries_variance.py::TestGarchStandaloneReference.
EGARCH uses the Nelson (1991) labelling (alpha=leverage, gamma=size),
identical to rugarch's, so no parameter swap is applied.

`uncvariance` is rugarch's reported unconditional variance (the
closed-form long-run Var(eps) implied by the fitted coefficients) --
the third-party oracle for copulax's stats()["unconditional_variance"]
accessor (TestUnconditionalVarianceThirdParty). sGARCH -> omega/(1 -
sum alpha - sum beta); iGARCH -> inf (does not exist, persistence=1);
gjrGARCH -> omega/(1 - alpha - beta - 0.5*gamma) (rugarch fixes
kappa=E[z^2 1{z<0}]=0.5 for all laws); eGARCH -> exp(omega/(1 - sum
beta)) (Nelson geometric-mean convention).
"""

